gEM(){return"RedVet AI is a clinical and educational support tool. It does not replace professional judgment, physical examination, diagnostic tests, anamnesis, patient follow-up, or the legal and ethical responsibility of the veterinarian.\n\nAI-generated diagnoses are only suggestions or possible differential diagnoses; they are not a definitive diagnosis. Treatment proposals, medications, routes of administration, doses, frequencies, duration, contraindications, or interactions may contain errors, omissions, incomplete, outdated, or patient-inapplicable information.\n\nBefore adding any AI-generated content to a medical record, prescription, medical instruction, client communication, or clinical decision, the veterinarian must review, correct, discard, or validate it according to examination, tests, clinical judgment, and applicable law. The final decision and its consequences are the exclusive responsibility of the treating or signing veterinarian.\n\nUsing this feature to diagnose, prescribe, indicate treatments, or provide dosages is strictly prohibited for anyone who is not legally authorized to practice veterinary medicine. Students, assistants, administrative staff, or other users may only use it for educational or internal support purposes, under supervision and express validation by a responsible veterinarian.\n\nIn Mexico, by way of reference, the Federal Animal Health Law and its Regulations reserve or require veterinary supervision for diagnosis, prevention, treatment, prescription, dosing, and administration of products for animal use; and the General Health Law requires a legally issued and registered professional degree to practice professional activities in veterinary medicine. If you practice in another country, you must comply with the applicable local regulations."},
